---
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { kinetics } from '../data/kinetics';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/site';
---

<section class="reproduction" id="reproduce" aria-labelledby="reproduce-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="reproduce-title">Run the insole workflow</h2>
  <p>Use Python 3.12 and the <SiteLink href={kinetics.release}>tagged code release {kinetics.version}</SiteLink>. The demo uses a small U-Net and synthetic signals to exercise the insole workflow on CPU without study data or pretrained weights.</p>
  <ol class="run-steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Get the release</h3>
      <pre><code>{kinetics.clone}</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Install and run the demo</h3>
      <p>Create an environment with <code>python -m venv .venv</code>. Activate it with <code>source .venv/bin/activate</code> on Linux or macOS, or <code>.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1</code> in PowerShell. Then run the following commands.</p>
      <pre><code>{kinetics.demo}</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Check the output</h3>
      <p>The command prints <code>Saved run: …/runs/demo_Fy_LL_UNet_…</code>. Open that directory and check that <code>status.json</code> reports <code>"status": "complete"</code>. The run also writes <code>summary.json</code> and fold-level predictions. Those results describe synthetic inputs.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Verified on CPU.</strong> A fresh checkout of {kinetics.version} completed the synthetic fold and produced finite reference and prediction arrays. The <SiteLink href={sitePath(kinetics.verificationPath)}>demo verification record</SiteLink> lists the tested versions, completion status, and expected array shape.</p>
  <h3>Work with the study data</h3>
  <p>Huawei Wang’s <SiteLink href={kinetics.dataUrl}>processed treadmill and insole recordings</SiteLink> are publicly downloadable. Use the <SiteLink href={kinetics.dataGuide}>data preparation guide</SiteLink> to create the expected input files. To reproduce the article evaluation, match the preprocessing, target scaling and participant folds described in the study.</p>
  <pre><code>{kinetics.inspect}</code></pre>
  <p>The article’s training-ready exports and pretrained checkpoints are separate from the release. The verification record covers synthetic inputs only.</p>
</section>
